Hi,
In the OSF1 (Digital Unix) posix threads package
there is a recursive mutex.
This is not supposed to be used
as the lock for a condition variable
because if recursion is > 1 
then the coniditional wait
will fail to unlock the mutex.
So fast mutexes are suggested.

However, for recursive mutexes,
why did the conditional not simply unlock 
the recursive mutex many times 
until it was free.  Store that number
on the stack.  On return pop the number
and lock it that many times.

rgs,
/Terence Cross.



