carson@tron.bwi.wec.com (Dana_Carson) writes:

>I'm trying to get the netpbm distribution running on a Digital Alpha
>running OSF1 V3.2.  It compiles and builds but seems to have a problem
>with xwd (at least) files. It complains that 
>xwdtopnm: unknown XWD file version: 33554432
>but xwdtopnm on another machine can deal with the same xwd file fine.
>Has anyone dealt with this problem and have patches for it?  I assume
>its a 64/32 bit problem on the Alpha. 

No, it's a 64/32 bit problem in the NetPBM source, which erroneously
assumes that sizeof(long) == sizeof(int).

>If I build with the compiler
>options to force 32 bit pointers the program core dumps.

It's not 64-bit pointers that's the problem. Fix netpbm/pnm/x11wd.h
to use 32-bit values for everything. Better yet would be to use the
X header file <X11/XWDFile.h> when possible.

--

