midboe@fly.HiWAAY.net (Matt Midboe) writes:

>We seem to get this "unable to process From lines [envelops]" error
>message from the Qualcomm POP3 server a lot. A lot, being maybe once a
>week one of our 3500+ users complains about it. Is this just a problem
>with file locking or what? What can I do to stop this from happening?

Not running Solaris are you?

If so, check the "From " lines of the mailbox of the user in question
- you may indeed find that they are not well formed.

If all of the above is true, then the culprit is /usr/lib/mail.local
as it is pretty simple-minded about constructing "From "
lines. Specificially, it doesn't cope with "From: " lines that have
the email address on a continuation line.

Being a good net-citizen, we reported this as a fault in 2.5, but the
support staff struggled to understand the problem since mailtool
worked (sigh), at that point we knew it was a lost-cause and cancelled
the fault call so I guess the problem will live on for some time.

I note that you've cross-posted in an OSF group, maybe they have
the same bug.


Regards.



