> H. S. R�pcke wrote:
> >
> > Hello,
> >
> > Is it possible to mount an tape-device remote,
> > which is attached to another maschine? I want
> > to make backups with the networker-tool from
> > Digital coming with DU 3.2C (BRXNSS...350 Subset).

Apart from there being no concept of mounting tape devices in UNIX, you don't 
access the tape drives remotely when using Networker.

After installing the client software on the systems to be backed up and the 
server software on the system with the tape drive, Networker will send the data 
from the clients to the server to be backed up. No (direct) remote tape drive 
access is involved.

Note that the license included with Digital UNIX won't allow you to back up any 
other systems: you can only back up the current system (hence, SingleServer 
Networker). Just obtain the PAKs and install them, and you'll have the 
full-blown Networker.
