Curt:
	If you're running Digital UNIX V3.* your choices are:
	
	1) With cc, you can implement mb() only via an asm.
	   See the Digital UNIX Programmer's Guide and/or
	   /usr/include/*asm*.h

	2) With cc -migrate, you can implement mb() using a builtin.
	   If you provide a prototype, then the compiler will recognize
	   the call as a builtin.  The prototype, (only for -migrate)
	   is 
		/*
		**  Memory Barrier
		*/
		void    __MB(void);

	Beginning with Digital UNIX V4.*, the -migrate compiler becomes
	the default compiler and it can handle asms(), so both approaches
	will work.  I don't know anything about the _mb symbol in libc.

Joe

