In article <4m096h$8m2@camelot.ccs.neu.edu>, mikeb@ccs.neu.edu (Michael Bukhin) writes:
>Frithjof Kruggel (kruggel@cns.mpg.de) wrote:
>: Perhaps trivial:
>: Did you install the CLC driver vsrion 3.0?
>
>That might be my problem.  I'm not exactly sure what the CLC driver is.
>I didn't think I needed any drivers for the tape drive..  Can you give
>me some pointers to this driver? thanks

I think I've already commented on the original problem, either by
mail or as a follow-up.  As to the CLC drivers.

The "CLC driver" is one of a pair of drivers for SCSI Medium Changer
devices and Optical devices.  CLC is CAM Layered Components, since the
underly SCSI subsystem is based on the Common Access Method (CAM).  The
two drivers are the MC driver for Medium changer devices and the OP
driver for Optical devices.

Both sets of drivers are on the Consolidated distribution, BUT they
are only licensed in conjunction with products that use them.  In the
case of the Medium Changer driver, it is licensed with NSR, HSM and
the Media Robot Utility.  Of these the Media Robot Utility is the
least expensive.  Supported DLT loaders and libraries, and the RDAT
loader (TLZ7L) should shipping with a copy of MRU included.

The MC driver is only needed to use the medium changer via host based
software.  It isn't needed to use the bare tape drive or the front
panel controls where provided.

