In article <4m1lf4$1qp@tst.hk.super.net>, cklo@news.hk.super.net 
(Mr Cheuk Kong Lo) writes:
>Is KZPSA-BB supporting only 7 SCSI target per controller? We encounter a
>8200 system with two controllers (isp0, isp1, are these KZPSA-BB??) and
>scu does not poll target >7 while show device at the boot prompt will see 
>disk at target 8.
>
>And we do not sure how to change the kernel config file to have target
>8.
>
>Do we have to config the controller for 15 targets operation?

The difference is what the KZPSA-BB card can do and what UNIX can do! The
KZPSA-BB can support the full range of FWD SCSI addresses but Digital UNIX 
does not at present support more than eight addresses per bus (ie controller
plus seven devices) 

On my 8400 system with KZPSA cards they show as controller pza0, pza1 etc.

