|>How do I get gdb to trap unaligned accesses (ie the equivalent of
|>0x<address>/i in dbx)?
|>

Chris,

   I don't know about gdb, but 0x<address>/i is generally used 
for displaying memory addresses and not for unaligned access trapping.

   The Ladebug debugger has a "catch unaligned" command that allows
you to trap unaligned accesses.  There's a corresponding "ignore
unaligned" command to turn unaligned access trapping off.  The default
is to ignore unaligned accesses.  

   This is covered in chapter 9 of the latest Ladebug documentation.    
