> I'm afraid I missed the beginning of this thread.  I've just got the
> documentation for dUnix 4.0 and it looks like they're using the same
> basic design for handling NIS/C2 which creates a bottleneck at the
> /var/yp/src/prpasswd file.  Any chance that DEC's tweaked the code so
> that this no longer causes major problems when a lot of people try to
> log in at one time? 

Nope.

The Version 4 SPD <ftp://ftp.digital.com/pub/Digital/info/SPD/41-61-13.txt>
includes the following disclaimer:

|  Support is provided for accessing NIS distributed databases while run-
|  ning Enhanced Security. NIS can also be used to distribute the Enhanced
|  Security protected password database. When using NIS, no more than 4000
|  user accounts are supported by the Enhanced Security subset. The num-
|  ber of simultaneous logins allowed is dependent on the configuration.

The 3.2D SPD, which is appended at the same URL says:

| o  Digital UNIX allows distribution of extended C2 security profil-
|    ing information over the network via the network information ser-
|    vices (NIS).

with no disclaimer I can find.

So, instead of tweaking the code, they've tweaked the SPD.

