Peter Gillham wrote:
> 
> What is the message "vmunix table is full" likely to mean ?
> Prior to this a "task create fail" message appeared.
> Our customer's system had been running fine until at some point these
> messages came up around the time we fork some extra temporary processes.

You may have run up to the limit of the number of process table entries
configured into the unix kernel. You can increase the number by editing
the /etc/sysconfigtab file, or using the sysconfig(8)/sysconfigdb(8)
commands to increase the max-proc-per-user attribute in the proc
subsystem, for example:

put these lines in /etc/sysconfigtab

proc:
        max-proc-per-user=128 

to increase the number of processes that can be created by a specific
user to 128. Then reboot. The default max-proc-per-user is 64. Note:
this increases the size of vmunix.



