 	Depending upon the laserjet, there are also a couple of additional
	options. You can:
	
		1) Install a network card in the printer allowing the alpha
		   to work normally, and if you cant print to a network
		   printer with windows, you can still attach it to the
		   parallel port of the PC.
		   
		2) You could also attach the printer to the parallel port
		   of the PC and use a serial line from the alpha. The 
		   hpIIIsi can print via a serial or parallel and a number
		   of others must be able to also. It may require manual
		   selection at the printer though. I only present these
		   options as additional ways of avoiding being dependent
		   on windows to get printing done. You won't think this
		   is being nit-picky after printing a page of postscript
		   bit mapped graphics only to watch part of the page print
		   before the black screen of death appears.
		   
