The error message suggests that rrz2c does not start at block 0 of the disk
(where you'll find the disklabel).  As your label shows, that is correct.  The
"c" partition has a non-zero offset.

Specify the "a" partition instead, which has a zero offset.

BTW - in current versions of Digital UNIX, you could just say:

disklabel -r rz2

disklabel would find an appropriate partition to open.

