In article <31746407.412F@teleport.com>, Rich Siegel <siegelr@teleport.com> writes:
>According to DUNIX documentation, the maximum number of tasks is 
>derived from max users.  However, the docs don't mention what the formula 
>is.  How can I determine what the current task limit is for a given max 
>users under DUNIX 3.2c
>

Depends on how you need to get the value.

$ dbx -k /vmunix
(dbx) p task_max
277

Will do it.

The formula, such as it, is in /usr/sys/conf/param.c. Look for
TASK_MAX. Personally, I can't wait until param.c is evaporated.
In V4.0, things like task_max, thread_max, and maxusers can
be set directly at boot time from /etc/sysconfigtab. No edit
config files and rebuiling the kernel to up the number of users, etc.


