	The current released versions of Digital UNIX do not support baud rates
higher than 38400 for it's serial ports. However, in the next release of
Digital UNIX (V4.0) the DEC 3000's will support up to 57600, the AlphaStations
and AlphaServers will support 57600 and 115200, and the DEC 2000's will only
support 38400.

	The reason that the DEC 2000 series only supports 38400 is because they
use the 16450 uart which only has a one byte buffer. You can however add an ISA
serial card to the system that has the 16550 uart and run those serial lines
at 57600 and 115200 on these systems.




