In article <4kk8o9$2ch@morgoth.sfu.ca>, rtmcbrid@sfu.ca (Ryan Thomas McBride) says:
>
>1) I have a GVC internal (ISA) modem. What do I have to do to get it to 
>work? (I've allready configured it with the ECU to generic isa modem). I 
>need to use it to connect to the internet using slip or PPP (preferably 
>PPP). Can anyone help me out or point me to a place where I can find more 
>information? 
>
>2) I also have a ISA sound card (SoundBlaster). Is there any way to get 
>it to work in the Alpha? If so, how?
>
>3) How would I go about setting my system up so that I could choose 
>between booting Unix and Windows NT?
>
1. read the man pages to "manual_slip_setup" (use "apropos manual")
   to configure your modem. Be sure DECunix will display the device
   during bootup (use "uerf -R -r 300 |more"). Check the firmware
   configuration using "show config" and "show device".

2. Use "isacfg" on the firmware prompt (look into the user guide
   "graphic option setup") and install the multimedia software kit
   (requires runtime licence)

3. You must install the ARP Console firmware on your system 
   (included on the firmware CD), see user guide for more information.
   You need 2 harddisks for the dualboot option because NT will
   create a special bootblock for its own

Regards

  Ralf 



