newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1,comp.sys.dec
x-mailer: Mozilla 2.01Ib7 (X11; I; OSF1 T4.0 alpha)

Timothy M. Wieman wrote:
> 
> Will Digital UNIX Ver. 4.0 support binary compatibility with Ver. 3.2?
> How about if the executables are compiled -nonshared?

Backwards compatibility is supported.  Newer releases are expected to
run executables built on older releases.  The opposite works sometimes
but isn't guaranteed.

In general you should also keep an eye on the release notes for
notices of retired features/interfaces that may impact binary
compatibility.  For example, in 4.0 there are a handful of math
routines which have been retired from libc due to their duplication
in libm.  If you find that you're relying on these interfaces
make sure that you're linking with libm on 3.2.

