With <31693E72.B4B@vfr.interceptor.com>,
it seems Thumper! (thumper@vfr.interceptor.com) sez:

+ I can't seem to get my crontab entry to suppress sending me mail.
+ 
+ I've tried 
+ 
+ 7 1 * * * /usr/sbin/ntpdate tick.usno.navy.mil 2>&1

Well, that point stderr at the same place as stdout.  Since stdout
is mailed to you along with the "usual" stderr, that really doesn't
change anything.


+ 7 1 * * * /usr/sbin/ntpdate tick.usno.navy.mil 2>/dev/null >/dev/null

That would seem to work.  You really shouldn't need that last
redirection, though; the 2> should do it.

+ and even tried by adding a 
+ MAILTO=/dev/null
+ line in the file.

Eeeeeuhhhh?  I've never heard of anything close to that before.
Either 1) you have a strange variant of OSF/1, or 2) you're doing
it wrong, or 3) I've just not seen it before yet.  :-)


You might also consider using the -s flag on ntpdate(8), which will
log via the syslog rather than writing to stdout.  This would
effectively solve the problem, unless what's being output are error
messages.


