#Is one of the DECNSR-NET-CLNT licenses supposed to go on the server?  If
#so, my supplier misinformed me (or I misunderstood him) and I'll have to get
#another, but I couldn't find anything in the documentation that said I had
#to have one of each license on the server.

Client licences reside on the NetWorker server system, both Digital
LMF PAKs or Legato enablers (used by many other types of NetWorker
server systems).  Some special licensing can take place on a NetWorker
client, but that is uncommon.  Relocate the client licenses onto the
NetWorker server system, do an 'lmf reset', shutdown nsr (if you 
haven't already), and restart nsrd.  You will need at least one client
license per client system you intend to back up registered on the 
NetWorker server, more should you be using archiving.  This should
be covered in the installation guide or (very likely) the SPD.

regards,

