Wuxu Peng (peng@infinite.cs.swt.edu) wrote:
: We just received an AlphaServer 2100 5/250.  The
: machine came with preinstalled software.  The
: timezone was set to EST.  I could not change it to
: CST.  The command "timezone" has no effect.  I am
: aware of the general "date" problem (In fact I had
: to reset the time after each reboot). Is this related
: to the "date" problem?

It has nothing to do with the date problem.  The timezone is controlled
by symbolic link /etc/zoneinfo/localtime.  If you look at this now you
should see something like:

# ls -l /etc/zoneinfo/localtime
lrwxr-xr-x   1 root     system        12 Jan 12 10:42 localtime -> ./US/Eastern

To change it, do

# cd /etc/zoneinfo
# rm localtime
# ln -s ./US/Central localtime

and there you are.

Martin
