 ___________________________________________________________________

 PRODUCT NAME:  Digital UNIX[R] Server Extensions,      SPD 44.35.12
                Version 4.0 (Digital UNIX V3.2D appended)

 DESCRIPTION

 Digital UNIX Server Extensions is a layered product for the Digital
 UNIX Operating System which provides server services for other sup-
 ported Digital UNIX systems.

 REMOTE INSTALLATION SERVICE (RIS)

 The Digital UNIX Server Extensions includes the Remote Installation
 Service (RIS). The RIS sets up a framework on a Digital UNIX server
 system which enables other Digital UNIX client systems to install the
 operating system software over the network from the server system. BOOTP
 is the boot protocol used to initiate the installations. Because of
 the high bandwidth requirements, RIS is supported only in local area
 network environments.

 A RIS client can be booted from the following interfaces:

 o  Internal Ethernet

 o  The PMAD TURBOchannel Ethernet option card

 o  The DE422 and DE425 EISA Ethernet option cards

 o  The DE203, DE204, and DE205 ISA Ethernet option cards

 o  The DE434, DE435, and DE436 PCI Ethernet option cards

 o  The DEFEA EISA family of FDDI option cards

 o  The DEFPA PCI family of FDDI option cards

                                                          March 1996


 

 o  The DEFTA TURBOchannel family of FDDI option cards

 o  The DETRA Token Ring option card

 RIS supports the installation of a Third Party or Foreign Graphics kit
 into the RIS area. This is useful in the case where the user has in-
 stalled a new graphics device into the system which has a driver that
 needs to be added to the system. With the driver included in the RIS
 area, the user can use the graphics device during installation.

 The server must be a Digital UNIX server. Support for installing from
 an ULTRIX RIS Server to a Digital UNIX client has been retired.

 The ability to remotely install ULTRIX clients from an ULTRIX server,
 as well as the ability to remotely install Digital UNIX clients from
 a Digital UNIX server will continue to be supported.

 DATALESS CONFIGURATIONS

 The Digital UNIX Server Extensions include support to install and op-
 erate systems with a dataless configuration. Dataless configurations
 have a minimum of one disk that is used for dumping, paging, and swap-
 ping. The root, /usr, and /var file systems are stored on the server
 system.

 The Dataless Management Utility (DMU) is provided for the Digital UNIX
 server system, enabling the server to register and manage the soft-
 ware areas used by Digital UNIX dataless clients. BOOTP is the pro-
 tocol used to boot the clients and mount the remote file systems.

 SYSTEM CLONING

 The Digital UNIX Server Extensions include the ability to duplicate
 the file system layout, file system type, and software subset selec-
 tions from identical systems already installed. Performing a cloned
 installation alleviates the need to answer most questions during the
 installation procedure. Installation cloning can only be performed us-
 ing RIS.


