     PRODUCT NAME:  Developers' Toolkit for Digital UNIX,   SPD 44.36.12
                    Version 4.0 

     DESCRIPTION

     The Developers' Toolkit for Digital UNIX[TM] provides a basic program
     development toolset for the Digital UNIX Operating System. This prod-
     uct combines the previous Developers' Toolkit and C Developers' Ex-
     tensions products into a single solution.

     The Developers' Toolkit for Digital UNIX[TM] provides a basic program
     development toolset for the Digital UNIX Operating System. This prod-
     uct combines the previous Developers' Toolkit and C Developers' Ex-
     tensions products into a single solution.

     The Developers' Toolkit for Digital UNIX[TM] is the basic toolkit for
     software development on Digital UNIX. It is the prerequisite for all
     development tools, languages, and environments. The Developers' Toolkit
     contains the following components:

     o  Two ANSI conformant C Compilers, including DEC C for Digital Unix

     o  Debuggers (ladebug, dbx)

     o  Program analysis tools (profiling and performance analysis)

     o  Porting Assistant

     o  Reordering tools (cord, feedback, runcord)

     The C Compilers

     The Developers' Toolkit offers two C compiler implementations.

     The default C language compiler is DEC C for Digital Unix, which was
     specifically developed and optimized for use with Alpha systems. The
     DEC C compiler is invoked with the cc command. In previous versions
     of Digital UNIX, DEC C was invoked with the cc -migrate command. The

                                                              March 1996






     Developers' Toolkit for Digital UNIX, Version 4.0      SPD 44.36.12


     cc -migrate command, which uses different default flags and libraries,
     is still supported.

     The default DEC C compiler offers improved optimization, additional
     features, and greater compatibility with Digital compilers on other
     platforms. DEC C is upwardly compatible with the previous compiler and
     the default flags are consistent. DEC C is also available on the Open-
     VMS operating system.

     While Digital recommends the use of DEC C, the previous C language com-
     piler is still available for a limited time. This compiler, which was
     the default C compiler in all previous versions of Digital UNIX, is
     invoked with the cc -oldc command.

     Both compilers are ANSI-compliant implementations of the C program-
     ming language with extended support for non-ANSI C dialects, perfor-
     mance tuning, and platform integration. They generate optimized position-
     independent code and support shared libraries.

     Both compilers generate complete debug and traceback records for use
     with the ladebug and dbx debuggers, which allows the C programmer to
     use the debuggers to set breakpoints, examine and modify the contents
