I've also had problems with Session Manager, but not with umask but with PATHs 
to application directories. It seems that session manager does not run the 
profile (or .cshrc and .login if you use csh) before starting up the 
application. One solution that works, but is somewhat crude, it to execute the 
$HOME/.profile before running the command; insert like:

sh -c ".profile; your_command" in the session managers options/define menu.

(I'm not 100% sure about the "-c". I'm at home. Look in man pages for sh).

Good luck!


