Hello !

Here are some more details about the pb.

. The command copy, in spite of the /verify option, does not see any pb; the following compare 
returns errors.

. The length of the smallest file with which I remarked truncation is 8956 byte. OSF's nfs server 
buffers are 8K length, OSF's pagesize is also 8K.

. For a given file, truncation is always the same : whatever the couple OS/2-OSF is, whenever the 
test is done, the missing part of the file is always the same. It ranges from 424 bytes for a 8K 
file to 114K for a 800K one.

. With a 32K file, I noticed a 2 x 2984 byte length truncation; 2984 is the size of the OS/2 
nfs-client buffers.

. This pb appears only with the couple OS/2 V 2.11 -> OSF V 3.0B; with an ufs volume or with an 
AdvFS + LSM (simple mirroring) one.

. Changing the size of nfs-client buffers (smaller or ajusted on the 8K of the OSF) does not fix 
the pb.

. If we double the load by adding a 2nd PC, the frequency of the pb seems to remain unchanged.

. During the tests, we checked that :
		- the Alpha was not (over)loaded
		- there was not nfs server error
		- Alpha's disk fragmentation remains very low
		- all the nfs daemons were up (no <defunct>).


I have an IP-trace (OS/2 side) were we can see this pb; the only difference with a "normal" case is 
that the OS/2 re-send 1 second after the previous send the missing part (and the dialog just before 
and just after this re-sending).


Thank you.
