Derek Hopkins (smstechs@smstechs.demon.co.uk) wrote:
: Hello,
: 
: I have a problem ftp'ing a file using ftp or rcp.
: 
: The file is over 2GB, OSF/1 will support this size (advfs also) and the
: local system is running fine. 

Try the following tricks that avoid command line tool internal limitations:

echo /abc/def/file.abc | cpio -oc | rsh other_host_name cpio -ic

The above will copy over the network and should not be limited to
some artificial limit on file size.

Ok, lets get closer to the metal:

cat -u </abc/def/file.abc | rsh other_host_name cat -u - >/new/machine/path/file.abc

Good luck.

